---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Illustration from '../components/Illustration.astro';
import SearchIcon from '../components/SearchIcon.astro';
import '../styles/patterns.css';
import { BETA_PATH } from '../config';
---
<Base title="How it works" description="How Sermount works: add a sermon, get the transcript, search everything your church has preached, and turn any sermon into the week's writing in the speaker's voice.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">How it works</p>
      <h1>From Sunday's sermon to something you can search on Monday.</h1>
      <p class="lead">You add the sermon. Sermount writes the transcript, makes it searchable and drafts the week's writing. Every sermon you add makes the archive more useful.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap steps">

      <div class="split step">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="step-no">01</p>
          <h2>Add a sermon</h2>
          <p>Upload the audio or video file, paste the YouTube link, or bring a transcript you already have as an SRT file. For a YouTube link you can set where the sermon starts and ends, so the welcome and announcements stay out.</p>
          <p>Say who preached it, when, and which series it belongs to.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- TODO demo-org screenshot: Upload Sermon, YouTube link -->
        <Illustration>
          <div class="frame form">
            <div class="tabs" aria-hidden="true"><span>File</span><span class="on">YouTube link</span><span>SRT</span></div>
            <div class="fields">
              <div class="field wide"><span class="f-label">YouTube link</span><span class="f-input">youtube.com/watch?v=…</span></div>
              <div class="field"><span class="f-label">Starts at</span><span class="f-input mono">00:21:40</span></div>
              <div class="field"><span class="f-label">Ends at</span><span class="f-input mono">01:04:15</span></div>
              <div class="field"><span class="f-label">Speaker</span><span class="f-input">Rev. Lena Marsh</span></div>
              <div class="field"><span class="f-label">Date</span><span class="f-input">17 Nov 2024</span></div>
              <div class="field wide"><span class="f-label">Series</span><span class="f-input">Questions Jesus Asked</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </Illustration>
      </div>

      <div class="split step">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="step-no">02</p>
          <h2>Sermount writes the transcript</h2>
          <p>Every word, with the time it was said. If a name or a word comes out wrong, fix that line by hand.</p>
          <p>Download the transcript as SRT for captions, or as plain text.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- TODO demo-org screenshot: transcript page -->
        <Illustration>
          <div class="frame">
            <div class="frame-bar"><span class="meta">Jesus Wept · Rev. Lena Marsh</span><span class="meta dl">Download SRT · TXT</span></div>
            <div class="transcript">
              <div class="line"><span class="meta">30:41</span><span>Martha goes out to meet him on the road. Mary stays in the house.</span></div>
              <div class="line"><span class="meta">30:52</span><span>Two sisters, the same grief, two completely different ways of carrying it.</span></div>
              <div class="line on"><span class="meta tc-on">31:02</span><span>Jesus knew Lazarus would walk out of that tomb, and he wept anyway.</span></div>
              <div class="line"><span class="meta">31:10</span><span>Don't let anyone hurry your tears.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </Illustration>
      </div>

      <div class="split step">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="step-no">03</p>
          <h2>Search everything you've preached</h2>
          <p>Ask the archive in plain words, the way you'd ask a colleague. Put a phrase in quotes to find those exact words. Narrow it to one speaker when you need to.</p>
          <p>Results show the line itself and the moment it was said. Open the transcript right there, or copy the excerpt. In the transcript of a YouTube sermon, a timecode opens the video at that moment.</p>
          <p class="coming"><span class="coming-tag">Coming</span> Before the beta opens: play the sermon inside Sermount, with the transcript following along.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- TODO demo-org screenshot: dashboard search with speaker filter -->
        <Illustration>
          <div class="frame">
            <div class="search"><SearchIcon /><span class="q">"don't let anyone hurry"</span><span class="filter">All speakers</span></div>
            <div class="group">
              <p class="group-title">Transcript hits</p>
              <div class="hit">
                <p class="meta"><span class="tc">31:10</span> · Rev. Lena Marsh, guest · 17 Nov 2024</p>
                <p><mark>Don't let anyone hurry</mark> your tears.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="hit">
                <p class="meta"><span class="tc">12:56</span> · Pastor Dan Okafor · 6 Jul 2023</p>
                <p>Healing has its own pace. <mark>Don't let anyone hurry</mark> you through it, including you.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </Illustration>
      </div>

      <div class="split step">
        <div class="copy">
          <p class="step-no">04</p>
          <h2>Make the week's writing</h2>
          <p>Each sermon gives you a set of drafts to edit, grouped the way a church office works:</p>
          <dl class="outputs-list">
            <div><dt>Comms</dt><dd>Blog, Newsletter, Sermon Brief</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Social</dt><dd>Reels, Quotes, Carousels, Anchor Moments</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Discipleship</dt><dd>Small Group, Devotionals</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p>Reels are the moments worth clipping, with their start and end times. Quote cards and carousels use your church's fonts and colours. Edit anything, then download it as a Word document or PDF.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- TODO demo-org screenshot: sermon page, Discipleship, Small Group -->
        <Illustration>
          <div class="frame">
            <div class="tabs" aria-hidden="true"><span>Comms</span><span>Social</span><span class="on">Discipleship</span></div>
            <div class="doc">
              <p class="meta">Small Group · Jesus Wept · John 11</p>
              <h3>Questions for this week</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Martha ran to Jesus and Mary stayed home. Which one sounds more like you when you're grieving?</li>
                <li>Jesus knew how the story would end and wept anyway. What does that say about your own tears?</li>
                <li>Who in your life has sat with you without trying to fix it?</li>
              </ol>
            </div>
          </div>
        </Illustration>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="voice">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Speaker Intelligence</p>
      <h2>Every output sounds like the speaker.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Churches have more than one voice. Your senior pastor, the youth pastor, the guest who preached in November. Sermount writes each sermon's newsletter, small-group guide and devotional in the voice of whoever preached it.</p>
      <p class="lead">So the newsletter after a guest Sunday sounds like the guest. The week after, it sounds like your pastor again.</p>
      <!-- TODO demo-org screenshot: two devotionals, two speakers -->
      <Illustration tone="night" class="letters-wrap">
        <div class="letters">
          <article class="letter">
            <p class="meta letter-meta"><span>Devotional</span><span>Josh Avery, youth pastor</span></p>
            <p>Real talk: Paul says he <em>learned</em> to be content. Learned. Nobody is born chill about not having stuff.</p>
            <p>Today, notice one thing you keep wanting. Don't fight it. Just hand it to God and see what's left.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="letter">
            <p class="meta letter-meta"><span>Devotional</span><span>Pastor Dan Okafor</span></p>
            <p>Paul wrote these words from a prison cell, which tells us contentment was never about the room he was in.</p>
            <p>Read Philippians 4:11-13 slowly this morning. Where have you been waiting for circumstances to change before you rest?</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </Illustration>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="label">More than one sermon at a time</p>
        <h2>Collections and plans</h2>
        <p>Group sermons into a Study Collection and Sermount writes a study guide or a devotional across all of them. Media Plans lay out a run of social posts on one topic, drawn from the Anchor Moments in your archive.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="label">Your team</p>
        <h2>Speakers and staff</h2>
        <p>Add every speaker who preaches, guests included, and archive the ones who move on. Invite staff with a link as editors, while one admin looks after the account, so the whole office works from one archive.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section closing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="close-box">
        <div>
          <h2>See it with your own sermons.</h2>
          <p class="lead">Sermount is in beta with a small group of churches. Tell us about yours.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn" href={BETA_PATH}>Join the beta</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .steps { display: grid; gap: 112px; }
  .step-no { font: 500 15px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--gold-text); margin: 0; }
  .step h2 { font-size: 36px; margin-top: -4px; }

  .tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; padding: 14px 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .tabs span { padding: 8px 12px 10px; }
  .tabs .on { color: var(--ink); box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--gold); font-weight: 500; }

  .fields { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px 20px; padding: 24px; }
  .field { display: grid; gap: 6px; min-width: 0; }
  .field.wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .f-label { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .f-input { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 15px; background: var(--paper); overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .f-input.mono { font: 500 14px/1.4 var(--mono); }

  .frame-bar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 14px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .dl { color: var(--gold-text); }

  .filter { margin-left: auto; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 10px; white-space: nowrap; }

  .coming { font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-soft); border-left: 2px solid var(--gold); padding-left: 14px; }
  .coming-tag { font: 500 12px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-text); margin-right: 6px; }

  .outputs-list { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 14px; }
  .outputs-list div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .outputs-list dt { font: 500 13px/1.6 var(--mono); letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .outputs-list dd { margin: 0; }

  .doc { padding: 22px 28px 28px; }
  .doc h3 { font: 400 24px/1.25 var(--serif); margin: 10px 0 14px; }
  .doc ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 12px; }

  .voice .lead + .lead { margin-top: 16px; }
  .voice :global(.letters-wrap) { margin-top: 64px; }

  .closing { padding-bottom: var(--section); }
  .close-box { border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 56px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 48px; align-items: end; }
  .close-box .lead { margin-top: 20px; }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .steps { gap: 72px; }
    .step h2 { font-size: 28px; }
    .fields { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; padding: 18px; gap: 12px 14px; }
    .tabs { padding: 10px 12px 0; }
    .search .filter { display: none; }
    .outputs-list div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; }
    .doc { padding: 18px; }
    .voice :global(.letters-wrap) { margin-top: 40px; }
    .close-box { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; padding-top: 40px; }
  }
</style>
